    "modified": true,
    "modifications": "4 real Interstate 5 and Lake Samish paths stitched through the OSM graph, heading Gaussian-smoothed, positions re-integrated from heading, then pinned back onto the real junctions (largest drift closed 43.2 m, spread back along each line), resampled at 2 m with curvature from the sampled positions; land elevation from 3DEP low-pass filtered, bridge decks synthesized (3DEP is bare earth); lanes simplified to the configured cross-section; junction connector roads synthesized (a turn, a straight and a turn)"
  },
  "meta": {
    "status": "live",
    "notes": "Interstate 5 southbound by Lake Samish, with the original rider shore choice and dedicated northbound access via Nulle Road and the Samish Way bridge. Source paths use OpenStreetMap and USGS bare-earth elevation; bridge decks, lanes, junction pieces and endpoint collars are synthesized for gameplay. Traffic-only access endpoint profiles adapt the bare-earth samples to their modeled host-road decks over authored 160 m spans; the Exit 246 shore endpoint adds 0.62 m to align the modeled crossing surface. Southbound ramp tails retain their forward lane; the shore core is shared by both directions."
  }
